{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":51,"timestamp":"2026-07-14T04:39:16.625440832Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f0a6a859-cba0-4308-948d-321479f4139a","title":"Plumb signing_enforcement into local CLI commands","description":"## Gap #1 — Enforcement Wiring (HIGH)\n\nCrosslink's signing_enforcement config key (disabled|audit|enforced) is read only in the server layer. The local CLI commands — commands/sync.rs, commands/kickoff/run.rs, commands/swarm/* — contain zero references to it.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Add enforcement gate adapter to each command path\n2. Make SignatureVerification::Invalid (from sync/trust.rs:429) a hard failure in enforced mode\n3. Add dry-run enum variant to signing_enforcement (<10 LOC)\n4. Check bootstrap.status == complete before rejecting (already built in sync/bootstrap.rs)\n5. Emit loud stderr + audit warning when enforcement is active but bootstrap incomplete\n\n## Effort\n~300 LOC. Thin per-command adapter, not a new monolithic VerificationService.\n\n## Source\nto-file/crosslink-gates/gates-issues.md Phase 1, GATE-1.2, GATE-1.4\ngates-verified-facts.md §2 (verified primitives)\n\n## Depends on\n- TDD BYPASS test suite (Phase 0 issue)\n- Crosslink repo prerequisites: #737 (driver key), #738 (bootstrap pending key)","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP/GaYGCIWHyqdSzALGPtsQqKm9VPhjnN+5xy9sAuZUcuP94eSnL/MlQQGinXmmC99ntGw0emWNFEvv/lMAEsAA="}
